+# Fact sheet · RINGANA BEYOND omega
+
+Accessed 2026-10-24. Primary sources:
+- **[P1]** Official product page, https://www.ringana.com/produkt/beyond-omega/?lang=en. Read in the browser with pwa-nav; the tab text (description, supplement facts, hero ingredients, use) was pasted by the user.
+- **[P2]** Official study PDF "The Influence of BEYOND omega on the Omega-3-Index", RINGANA GmbH, https://rin-wp-media.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/2024/10/Studienergebnisse_omega_EN.pdf (linked from P1 "Read more").
+- **[EU]** EU Reg. 432/2012 authorised health claims (also quoted in P2 p.1 with the 250 mg conditions).
+
+The product page is the primary source for product facts, so they count as verified. The study is RINGANA's own (n=27, no peer review, self-test dried blood spot analysed by an external lab), so its figures must be attributed on screen.
+
+| ID | Fact | Screen phrasing | Sources | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| F1 | Product: RINGANA CAPS BEYOND omega, softgel capsules, 60 per container (20 days). | "RINGANA BEYOND omega" | P1 | verified |
+| F2 | EPA and DHA come from microalgae oil (Schizochytrium sp.), a vegan source; "Omega-3—Without the Fish." | "Omega 3 without fish: from microalgae" | P1 | verified |
+| F3 | Daily serving = 3 capsules with meals and water: 960 mg EPA+DHA (640 mg DHA + 320 mg EPA), 1,042 mg total omega-3. | "960 mg EPA + DHA a day" | P1 (supplement facts) | verified |
+| F4 | Also contains vitamin D3 20 mcg (100 % DV), vitamin E 23.5 mg, vitamin K2 75 mcg, ubiquinol (CoQ10) 48 mg, astaxanthin 6 mg, lutein 10 mg, zeaxanthin 2 mg. | "+ vitamins D3, K2 & E" | P1 | verified |
+| F5 | EPA and DHA contribute to normal heart function (≥250 mg/day EPA+DHA). | "Normal heart function" | P1, P2, EU | verified |
+| F6 | DHA contributes to normal brain function (≥250 mg/day DHA). | "Normal brain function" | P1, P2, EU | verified |
+| F7 | DHA helps maintain normal vision (≥250 mg/day DHA). P1 adds that lutein, zeaxanthin and astaxanthin "support eye health". | "Normal vision" | P2, EU (DHA); P1 (carotenoids) | verified (use the DHA wording) |
+| F8 | Vitamin D3 supports normal immune system function. | "Immunity" | P1, EU | verified |
+| F9 | Vitamin K2 supports bone health. | "Bones" | P1, EU | verified |
+| F10 | Vitamin E contributes to protecting cells from oxidative stress. | "Cells" | P1, EU | verified |
+| F11 | Ubiquinol supports cellular energy production. | "Cellular energy" | P1 (marketing wording; not an EU-authorised claim) | uncertain, don't use on screen |
+| F12 | In RINGANA's study (27 people, 3 caps/day), the average Omega-3 Index rose 44.6 % after 20 days and 63.5 % after 90 days (4.84 % → 7.87 %); a control group of 9 stayed flat (4.79 → 4.97). | "+63.5% Omega-3 Index in 90 days*" | P2 p.3–4 | verified as RINGANA's own study; attribute on screen |
+| F13 | Optimal Omega-3 Index range is 8–12 %; the average in Spain is 6.55 %. | "Optimal: 8–12%" | P2 p.2 (citing Schuchardt et al. 2024, Omega-3 world map) | verified |
+| F14 | The study's omega-6:omega-3 ratio improved 29.2 % at 20 days and 36.9 % at 90 days (8.4:1 → 5.3:1). | not on screen | P2 | verified (study) |
+| F15 | In the study questionnaire, 93 % rated it very tolerable and 92 %+ noticed no aftertaste. | optional "93% found it very tolerable*" | P2 p.5 | verified as self-reported |
+
+## Myths and claims not to use
+- "Prevents/treats heart disease", "anti-inflammatory", "fights depression", "extends life": P2's background mentions these as research areas, but they are not authorised claims. The US label says the product is "not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease".
+- "Free of heavy metals": not stated on P1.
+- Triglycerides (2 g/day) and blood pressure (3 g/day): the product provides 960 mg, below those doses.
+- Don't present F12 as independent science; say "RINGANA study".
+
+## Disclaimer for the video
+"Food supplement. Not a substitute for a varied diet or medical advice. Adults only. *RINGANA internal study, 27 participants, 2024."
